            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0245" n="1079" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1079"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/10727a suppl.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-18T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 18, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2883. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 1643. Frothingham. Supplementing Department’s 2550, our 1538, October 31, 7
                    p.m., Embassy’s 3618, your 1846, November 11. In our view licenses are allowed
                    at discretion as exceptions to general rule of prohibition because of the
                    special circumstances of each particular case. Submission of copies of
                    permissions after allowance is not helpful because not practicable to deduce
                    therefrom any general rule to govern exceptional cases. Desirable that there be
                    harmony of action secured through conference as cases arise rather than protest
                    after action taken.</p>
                <p>Your suggestion respecting imports from northern neutrals corresponds to present
                    practice.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
